Z||000003||mrfiero||12-05-2000||11:50 PM||||The TH125-C tranny (3sp. auto. w/lockup torque convertor) used in the Fiero and most GM cars in the 80's is very reliable, but not very performance oriented.  <P>If you are wanting a more sporty feel, look for one with a 4 or 5 speed stick.  However, you won't have any of those nasty clutch issues with the auto.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
